Hi,

When trying to trap() arrivals, some of the arrivals are dropped from the simulation and finished is set to TRUE whereas I want to trap() them and have them wait() for a signal. Upon getting the signal and joining some trajectory() I immediatly untrap() the arrivals from the signal. My data contains around 6k arrivals, for about a 100 arrivals (not particularly different from the others) this occurs. It does not necessarily occur for the same arrivals when running the simulation multiple times. See:

The arrival times are unique for each arrival:

In the example below, job5680 is unable to trap() whereas 5681 is able to do it.
Log:
1401.45: job5680: now in region1QueueTraject
[1] "now in determine_if_wait_region1"
[1] "ended up in else if"
[1] "length of regionqueue is 21"
1401.45: job5680: Returned a 2, my id is: 5680

1401.45: job5681: now in region2QueueTraject
[1] "now in determine_if_wait_region2"
[1] "ended up in else if"
[1] "length of regionqueue is 21"
1401.45: job5681: Returned a 2, my id is: 5681
[1] "going to set my signal to 5681"
1401.45: job5681: now in wait region 2

Code:

determine_if_wait_region1 <- function(){
  print("now in determine_if_wait_region1")
  availablePickersRegion1 <<- get_capacity(env, "pickOperatorRegion1") - get_server_count(env, "pickOperatorRegion1")
  if(availablePickersRegion1 > 0 && nrow(regionqueue1_df) >= 1) {
    print("going to increase winq")
    increase_WINQ()
    print("increased winq!")
    remove_job_from_regionqueu1()
    return(1)
  }
  else if (availablePickersRegion1 == 0 && nrow(regionqueue1_df) >= 1){
    print("ended up in else if")
    print(paste("length of regionqueue is", nrow(regionqueue1_df)))
    return(2)
  }
 }

set_signal <- function(){
  print(paste("going to set my signal to", get_attribute(env, "id")))
  signal <- paste("Request for job with id", get_attribute(env, "id"))
  return(signal)
 }

pickingRegion1Trajectory <- trajectory("Picking Process") %>%
  untrap(function() set_signal()) %>%
  log_(function() paste("Now in picking traject", get_attribute(env, "region")))

region1QueueTraject <- trajectory("Arrivals looping in queue unless the arrival is the optimal arrival") %>%
  log_("now in region1QueueTraject") %>%
  branch(function() determine_if_wait_region1(),
         continue=c(TRUE, TRUE),
         pickingRegion1Trajectory,
         trajectory() %>%
          log_(function() paste("Returned a 2, my id is:", get_attribute(env, "id"))) %>%
           trap(function() set_signal(), trajectory() %>% log_("Got a signal!") %>% join(pickingRegion1Trajectory), interruptible=FALSE) %>%
         log_("now in wait region 1") %>%
         wait()
  )

